Pawline includes third-party components:

Needle3 model weights (needle3.cact)
  Source: https://huggingface.co/Cactus-Compute/needle3
  License: Apache License 2.0

cactus runtime, prebuilt static library (libcactus.a)
  Source: https://github.com/cactus-compute/cactus
  License: Apache License 2.0
  Note: the cactus *engine source repository*
  (https://github.com/cactus-compute/engine) is under a restricted
  license; only the prebuilt Apache-2.0 binaries are used here.

Both are used under the terms of the Apache License, Version 2.0
(http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).

pawline-native (0.2.0-beta) statically links LLVM libc++, libc++abi and libunwind
(Apache License 2.0 with LLVM Exceptions, https://llvm.org/LICENSE.txt) and embeds
the Liberation Sans 2.1.5 font (SIL Open Font License 1.1, https://openfontlicense.org/).
Correction: builds before this change (including v0.2.1-beta) embedded Liberation Sans 1.07.4, which is
licensed under the GNU GPL v.2 with Red Hat font exceptions, not the OFL.
Rust dependencies: smithay-client-toolkit (MIT), tiny-skia (BSD-3-Clause), fontdue (MIT/Apache-2.0).

Design reference (no code or assets copied)
Pawline's window and orb design was inspired by Nus Companion
(https://github.com/potlakai/nus-companion, Apache License 2.0). Nus Companion is a
Windows Electron app (JavaScript, CSS); Pawline is Rust drawn with tiny-skia, uses its own
palette, and contains no source files, images or fonts from that project (checked by file hash
and colour values at 3128b19). If code or assets from it are ever adapted, its licence text and
copyright notices (including those in its THIRD-PARTY.md) must be added here first.
